        {
          "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the numbers \\(3339\\), \\(2961\\), and \\(1491\\), we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of zero. The last non-zero remainder is the GCD.",
