          "token_end": 72,
          "check": "unknown",
          "claim": null,
          "prm": 0.9907271862030029,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "First, let's find the GCD of \\(3339\\) and \\(2961\\).",
          "token_start": 72,
          "token_end": 95,
          "check": "unknown",
          "claim": null,
          "prm": 0.9994632601737976,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Divide \\(3339\\) by \\(2961\\) and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   3339 = 2961 \\cdot 1 + 378\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(378\\).",
          "token_start": 95,
          "token_end": 156,
          "check": "true",
          "claim": "3339 = 2961 \\cdot 1 + 378",
          "prm": 0.9987523555755615,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. Now, apply the Euclidean algorithm to \\(2961\\) and \\(378\\):\n   \\[\n   2961 = 378 \\cdot 7 + 105\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(105\\).",
          "token_start": 156,
          "token_end": 218,
          "check": "false",
          "claim": "2961 = 378 \\cdot 7 + 105",
          "prm": 0.9699382781982422,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. Next, apply the Euclidean algorithm to \\(378\\) and \\(105\\):\n   \\[\n   378 = 105 \\cdot 3 + 63\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(63\\).",
          "token_start": 218,
          "token_end": 276,
          "check": "true",
          "claim": "378 = 105 \\cdot 3 + 63",
          "prm": 0.9997456669807434,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. Then, apply the Euclidean algorithm to \\(105\\) and \\(63\\):\n   \\[\n   105 = 63 \\cdot 1 + 42\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(42\\).",
          "token_start": 276,
          "token_end": 332,
          "check": "true",
          "claim": "105 = 63 \\cdot 1 + 42",
          "prm": 0.9996695518493652,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. Finally, apply the Euclidean algorithm to \\(63\\) and \\(42\\):\n   \\[\n   63 = 42 \\cdot 1 + 21\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(21\\).",
          "token_start": 332,
          "token_end": 386,
          "check": "true",
          "claim": "63 = 42 \\cdot 1 + 21",
          "prm": 0.9995342493057251,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "6. Apply the Euclidean algorithm to \\(42\\) and \\(21\\):\n   \\[\n   42 = 21 \\cdot 2 + 0\n   \\]\n   So, the remainder is \\(0\\).",
          "token_start": 386,
          "token_end": 436,
          "check": "true",
          "claim": "42 = 21 \\cdot 2 + 0",
          "prm": 0.9998413324356079,
          "prm_label": "true"
        },
        {
          "text": "The last non-zero remainder is \\(21\\). Therefore, the GCD of \\(3339\\) and \\(2961\\) is \\(21\\).",
